---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Contour from '../components/Contour.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Services — Next Steppe" description="Site analysis, planting design and design-build for xeric and native landscapes in the Vail Valley.">
  <section class="wrap services">
    <span class="eyebrow">Services</span>
    <h1>What a project includes</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Every project starts from the same reading of the site: where water arrives and
      leaves, how much sun each bed actually gets under the trees and the ridge, and what
      the elevation and fire rules allow within reach of the house. What comes after
      depends on how far you want to take it.
    </p>

    <div class="svc-list">
      <div class="svc card">
        <span class="tag">01</span>
        <h2>Site analysis</h2>
        <p>
          Elevation, slope and aspect from USGS terrain data; hours of direct sun per bed from
          lidar, with the trees and buildings in it; soils, flood mapping and wildlife range.
          Delivered as a site analysis sheet with a palette of species that suit each zone.
        </p>
        <p class="fit">Useful before you hire anyone, or before you plant anything yourself.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc card">
        <span class="tag">02</span>
        <h2>Planting design</h2>
        <p>
          The site analysis, plus a water plan, a planting plan with every plant placed, a
          planting schedule with counts and container sizes, a maintenance plan, and a concept
          rendering over a photo of your site on request. Ready to hand to an installer or to
          plant yourself.
        </p>
        <p class="fit">Pairs with Eagle County&rsquo;s Beyond Lawn turf-replacement program.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc card">
        <span class="tag">03</span>
        <h2>Design + install</h2>
        <p>
          The design, carried through: soil preparation, planting and mulch, sequenced so the
          beds go in during the short window the valley gives you. Scoped from the plan, with a
          written quote before any work starts.
        </p>
        <p class="fit">For beds and borders, HOA common areas and small public sites.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="pricing">
      Fees are set per project once the site has been seen. Cost ranges in a design are for
      budgeting, never a bid.
    </p>

    <div class="cta">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn primary">Start a project</a>
      <a href="/plants" class="btn">Read your own site in the plant browser</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Contour />

  <section class="wrap community-band">
    <span class="eyebrow">This Winter</span>
    <h2>One free design for a community site</h2>
    <p>
      A school, library, church, community garden or town parcel in the Vail Valley.
      Designed over the winter, ready to build next summer.
    </p>
    <a href="/community" class="btn">See the offer</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .services { padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 3rem; }
  .lead { max-width: 660px; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--basalt-soft); }
  .svc-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1.4rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .svc { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .svc h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
  .svc p { margin: 0; color: var(--basalt); }
  .svc .tag { align-self: flex-start; }
  .fit { color: var(--basalt-soft) !important; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: auto !important; padding-top: 0.8rem; }
  .pricing { margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--basalt-soft); max-width: 640px; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .community-band { padding-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .community-band p { max-width: 600px; color: var(--basalt-soft); }
</style>
